  M('shape-features', 'A shape keeps its own name', 'geometry', 6, 'g2-shape-parts', ['2.G.A.1'], 'Identify shapes by sides, corners, and equal square faces.', 'Recognize common flat and solid shapes.', 'A pentagon has five straight sides and five corners. Turning it does not change those features. A cube has six equal square faces.', 'Which features stay the same when a shape turns?', 'Find a hexagon and a cube together; describe what makes each one.'),
  M('square-tiles', 'A floor made from tiny squares', 'geometry', 6, 'g2-shape-parts', ['2.G.A.2'], 'Partition a rectangle into equal rows and columns of unit squares.', 'Keep rows and columns the same size.', 'A rectangle split into 3 rows and 4 columns contains 12 same-size squares. Cover each space once.', 'How do the rows keep the count organized without gaps?', 'Draw a rectangle with two rows of five squares and count it in two ways.'),
  M('fair-ribbons', 'Halves, thirds, and fourths for friends', 'fractions', 6, 'g2-shape-parts', ['2.G.A.3'], 'Partition one whole into two, three, or four equal shares and name one share.', 'Distinguish a whole from its equal-sized pieces.', 'Three equal shares make thirds. One share is one third, and all three thirds make the whole.', 'What must be equal before we can call the pieces thirds?', 'Fold identical paper ribbons into halves and fourths, keeping the whole fixed.'),
  M('same-share', 'Different cuts, the same fair share', 'fractions', 6, 'g2-shape-parts', ['2.G.A.3'], 'Recognize equal shares of the same whole even when the pieces have different shapes.', 'Name halves and fourths of a fixed whole.', 'One half of a rectangle can be a tall piece or a wide piece. A change in shape does not change its share when both cover half the same whole.', 'How can you compare the shares when the pieces look different?', 'Cut two equal paper rectangles into halves in different directions and compare the areas.')
